iterations.reply:
The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`. The platform team's approval of an http-client grant isn't reflected in the node's actual authority (the `with` clause), so importing it is not permitted regardless of that approval — the component must import exactly what the `with` clause grants. I'm reverting to the original, correct scope.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

